        "point": "Perlmann places B005 first because chaperonin-assisted folding is a fundamental, mature discovery with unusually compact and defensible attribution to Hartl and Horwich.",
        "response": "I agree that B005 has an exceptionally attractive attribution case and is a serious alternative. I give B035 the edge because its foundational physiology has also produced a highly consequential, established therapeutic transformation; its less tidy attribution remains the principal reason to keep B005 close."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "el-manira-abdel",
        "point": "El-Manira places B041 first, emphasizing the mature and globally important prevention of HPV infection and related cancers by virus-like particle vaccines.",
